---
/**
 * SteamLens system diagram — the arc's establishing shot on /projects/steam-lens/.
 *
 * Ported from the project repo's `mocks/m1_pipeline_figure_web.html`, which stays the
 * source of the *content*; this file owns how it behaves on the site. Two rules carried
 * over from there, both load-bearing:
 *
 *  - No measurements. F1s, costs and counts-that-move live in the prose and the report,
 *    so a living page can never contradict a frozen artifact. Structural identities
 *    (51 pinned aspects, the 250-review gold set, 49 games, batch N=10) stay: they are
 *    design facts, not instrument readings.
 *  - Built and planned are visually distinct. Solid panels are built and measured;
 *    the dashed rail is roadmap, labelled as not claimed.
 *
 * Every class is `p-` prefixed: the figure's natural names (card, desc, rule, node)
 * collide with the site's globals in Base.astro.
 */
---

<figure class="p-fig">
  <div class="p-scroll">
    <div class="p-canvas">
      <header class="p-head">
        <h2 class="p-h1">
          SteamLens · the system as it stands
          <span>Milestone 1 built &amp; measured</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="p-sub">
          From raw Steam reviews to per-game numbers: the model call is the smallest part;
          the instrument around it is the work.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="p-stages">
        <section class="p-panel p-s1">
          <div class="p-ph"><span class="p-num">1</span><h3>Data</h3></div>
          <div class="p-node">
            <b>Review corpus</b><span>49 games · raw Steam reviews</span>
          </div>
          <div class="p-down">↓</div>
          <div class="p-node">
            <b>Usable filter</b><span>English, Unicode-honest non-empty — the usable pool, counted exactly</span>
          </div>
          <div class="p-down">↓</div>
          <div class="p-node">
            <b>Store (SQLite / WAL)</b><span>migration runner · ingest asserts the census size before any spend</span>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="p-panel p-s2">
          <div class="p-ph"><span class="p-num">2</span><h3>Labeling engine</h3></div>
          <div class="p-node">
            <b>Census driver</b><span>resume by construction · three-pass failure sweep · circuit breakers</span>
          </div>
          <div class="p-down">↓</div>
          <div class="p-node">
            <b>Classify prompt (codebook v2)</b><span>51 pinned aspects · reviews cross as data-never-instructions · batch N=10</span>
          </div>
          <div class="p-down">↓</div>
          <div class="p-node">
            <b>Provider seam</b><span>raw httpx, no SDKs · budget reserved before dispatch · spend ledger</span>
          </div>
          <div class="p-down">↓</div>
          <div class="p-node">
            <b>Label pool + response archive</b><span>version-keyed envelopes · raw output content-addressed, never re-paid</span>
          </div>
          <p class="p-stat"><b>One disclosed provider refusal</b> kept in the artifact's arithmetic</p>
        </section>

        <section class="p-panel p-s3">
          <div class="p-ph"><span class="p-num">3</span><h3>Number mint</h3></div>
          <div class="p-node">
            <b>Survey-origin ∩ version pin</b><span>only origin-tagged survey labels under the pinned versions fold</span>
          </div>
          <div class="p-down">↓</div>
          <div class="p-node">
            <b>Per-game aspect aggregates</b><span>empties in the denominator · raw tallies, no floor</span>
          </div>
          <p class="p-stat"><b>Every displayed number</b> mints here · nowhere else</p>
          <p class="p-wall">
            <b>THE WALL</b> stories never mint numbers; an import-graph test + origin
            predicate keep it standing
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="p-panel p-s4">
          <div class="p-ph"><span class="p-num">4</span><h3>Evaluation instrument</h3></div>
          <div class="p-node">
            <b>Human gold set · 250 reviews</b><span>blind-labeled before any model output · versioned in the repo</span>
          </div>
          <div class="p-down">↓</div>
          <div class="p-node">
            <b>Certification of the bought labels</b><span>scored against gold · bootstrap CIs, resampled by review</span>
          </div>
          <div class="p-down">↓</div>
          <div class="p-node">
            <b>LLM judge · different family</b><span>an independent second annotator · calibrated against gold before use</span>
          </div>
          <div class="p-down">↓</div>
          <div class="p-node">
            <b>Census-sample agreement</b><span>a seeded n=1,000 sample · no evidence of a quality cliff outside gold</span>
          </div>
          <p class="p-stat">
            <b>Quote audit: zero non-verbatim spans</b> in storage · misattribution audit:
            human, in progress
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="p-panel p-s5">
          <div class="p-ph"><span class="p-num">5</span><h3>Evals gate CI</h3></div>
          <div class="p-node">
            <b>Committed fixture</b><span>both runs of record, rebuilt through the real writer surfaces</span>
          </div>
          <div class="p-down">↓</div>
          <div class="p-node">
            <b>Deterministic re-score</b><span>no fresh model output · catches code / scorer / artifact drift</span>
          </div>
          <div class="p-down">↓</div>
          <div class="p-node">
            <b>Exact-digit gate</b><span>a digit mismatch fails the build · deliberate change = scorer bump + pins re-exported, same commit</span>
          </div>
        </section>

        <aside class="p-rail">
          <div class="p-railbox">
            <h3>Built, waiting</h3>
            <div class="p-node">
              <b>Steam review client</b><span>the live door: resolve · histogram · windowed fetch — built and live-smoked; on the production path at deployment</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="p-railbox p-ghost">
            <h3>Next · not built</h3>
            <div class="p-node"><b>sampling study</b></div>
            <div class="p-down">↓</div>
            <div class="p-node"><b>deployed app</b></div>
            <div class="p-down">↓</div>
            <div class="p-node"><b>report chat (grounded)</b></div>
            <p class="p-railnote">dashed = roadmap, deliberately not claimed as built</p>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>

      <div class="p-support">
        <span class="p-slabel">Standing services</span>
        <span><b>Provenance stamps</b> · run id · code sha · config hash</span>
        <span><b>Budget caps</b> · atomic reserve-before-dispatch</span>
        <span><b>Typed errors</b> · world-failing vs promise-keeping never blur</span>
        <span><b>Narration sink</b> · every stage emits typed progress</span>
        <span><b>Politeness</b> · one retry-GET chokepoint owns the rate budget</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <figcaption class="p-cap">
    <strong>The instrument around the model.</strong> Solid panels are built and measured;
    the dashed rail is roadmap, not claimed as built. Honest limits: one human annotator,
    disclosed in every artifact; codebook v2 was tuned on gold, so v2-on-gold numbers stay
    development-grade until a fresh holdout lands; labels re-certify after any re-buy.
    Scores, intervals and costs live in the text and the report, not in this diagram.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  /* Stage hues sit in one lightness band around the site's blue and amber, so no stage
     shouts louder than another. */
  .p-fig {
    --p1: #7fa8c9;
    --p2: #e0a458;
    --p3: #8fbf9f;
    --p4: #a49add;
    --p5: #cf93a8;
    /* Break out of the 720px prose column: five stages need room the text doesn't.
       Width is capped so it stays a figure rather than a banner, and the viewport
       calc leaves a gutter so it never touches the edges or triggers page scroll. */
    width: min(1360px, calc(100vw - 40px));
    margin: 30px 0 34px;
    margin-left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
  }

  /* A safety net only — the wrapping grid below should never need it. */
  .p-scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
    overscroll-behavior-x: contain;
  }
  .p-canvas {
    border: 1px solid var(--hair);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--card);
    padding: 20px 22px 22px;
  }

  .p-head {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair);
    padding-bottom: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .p-h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 21px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--bright);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
  .p-h1 span {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 0.8em;
    white-space: nowrap;
    margin-left: 0.35em;
  }
  .p-h1 span::before {
    content: '— ';
  }
  .p-sub {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 6px 0 0;
    max-width: 78ch;
  }

  /* Stages wrap instead of insisting on one row: six tracks at a wide viewport,
     folding to three, two, then one as the width drops. The numbered chips carry the
     order, so a wrapped row still reads 1 → 5 without arrows between columns. */
  .p-stages {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(196px, 1fr));
    align-items: stretch;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .p-panel {
    border: 1.5px solid;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--paper);
    padding: 12px 11px 13px;
  }
  .p-s1 { border-color: #46566b; }
  .p-s2 { border-color: #6b5a40; }
  .p-s3 { border-color: #47604f; }
  .p-s4 { border-color: #575071; border-width: 2.5px; }
  .p-s5 { border-color: #6b4d58; }

  .p-ph {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 11px;
  }
  .p-ph h3 {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .p-num {
    width: 22px;
    height: 22px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    flex: none;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    color: var(--paper);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .p-s1 .p-num { background: var(--p1); }
  .p-s2 .p-num { background: var(--p2); }
  .p-s3 .p-num { background: var(--p3); }
  .p-s4 .p-num { background: var(--p4); }
  .p-s5 .p-num { background: var(--p5); }
  .p-s1 h3 { color: var(--p1); }
  .p-s2 h3 { color: var(--p2); }
  .p-s3 h3 { color: var(--p3); }
  .p-s4 h3 { color: var(--p4); }
  .p-s5 h3 { color: var(--p5); }

  .p-node {
    border: 1px solid var(--hair);
    border-radius: 9px;
    background: var(--card);
    padding: 9px 10px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .p-node b {
    display: block;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 650;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--bright);
  }
  .p-node span {
    display: block;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin-top: 3px;
  }
  .p-down {
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .p-stat {
    margin: 10px 0 0;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--hair);
    padding: 8px 10px;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .p-stat b { color: var(--bright); }

  /* the two-track wall, inverted to the site's light plate — the one deliberate shout */
  .p-wall {
    margin: 10px 0 0;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    padding: 9px 10px;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .p-wall b {
    display: block;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-size: 11px;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
  }

  .p-rail {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .p-railbox {
    border: 1.5px dashed var(--border);
    border-radius: 11px;
    background: var(--paper);
    padding: 11px;
  }
  .p-railbox h3 {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .p-ghost { opacity: 0.62; }
  .p-ghost .p-node {
    border-style: dashed;
    background: transparent;
  }
  .p-railnote {
    font-size: 10.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 7px 0 0;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .p-support {
    margin-top: 16px;
    border: 1.5px dashed #b97f35;
    border-radius: 11px;
    padding: 11px 14px;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 8px 22px;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .p-support .p-slabel {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--amber);
  }
  .p-support b {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .p-cap {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 12px;
    max-width: 74ch;
  }
  .p-cap strong { color: var(--ink); }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .p-canvas {
      padding: 16px 14px 18px;
    }
    .p-h1 {
      font-size: 18px;
    }
    .p-h1 span {
      white-space: normal;
    }
    /* Full-bleed stops earning its keep once the column is the whole screen. */
    .p-fig {
      width: 100%;
      margin-left: 0;
      transform: none;
    }
  }
</style>
